From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: leave native Prospero SIGSYS at syscall return site

Prospero SIGSYS can also report a native libkernel syscall failure. Do not
feed its errno/result in RAX to Wine's Windows syscall dispatcher: that turned
0xffffffffade97eba into win32u syscall 3770 and looped on illegal instruction.
The native syscall context already points after the syscall instruction, where
libkernel's wrapper handles the returned error. Windows syscall IDs are
zero-extended 13-bit values (ntdll or win32u table), so route only those.

---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -3267,5 +3267,18 @@ static void sigsys_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *_sigcontext )
     ERR_(seh)("Prospero SIGSYS code=%d errno=%d rax=%016lx rip=%016lx frame=%p frame_id=%08x frame_rip=%016lx\n",
               siginfo ? siginfo->si_code : 0, siginfo ? siginfo->si_errno : 0,
               (unsigned long)RAX_sig(sigcontext), (unsigned long)RIP_sig(sigcontext), frame,
               frame ? frame->syscall_id : 0, frame ? (unsigned long)frame->rip : 0);
+
+    /* Native libkernel wrappers can also raise SIGSYS. In that case RAX is
+     * the host syscall result, not a Wine service number; the saved RIP is
+     * already after the syscall and must be allowed to take the wrapper's
+     * error path. Wine's ntdll/win32u service IDs fit in 13 zero-extended
+     * bits (the table selector is bit 12). */
+    if ((ULONG_PTR)RAX_sig(sigcontext) > 0x1fff)
+    {
+        ERR_(seh)("Passing native Prospero SIGSYS through: rax=%016lx rip=%016lx flags=%08lx\n",
+                  (unsigned long)RAX_sig(sigcontext), (unsigned long)RIP_sig(sigcontext),
+                  (unsigned long)EFL_sig(sigcontext));
+        return;
+    }
 #endif
 
     TRACE_(seh)("SIGSYS, rax %#lx, rip %#lx.\n", (long)RAX_sig(sigcontext), (long)RIP_sig(sigcontext));
-- 
2.43.0
